{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Thus shall you bless</b> — to invoke merit: \"I and the lad will walk thus far\"; \"thus shall be your seed\"; and this is \"that thus far HaShem has blessed me.\" And 25 letters in the verse Shema Yisra'el, and 25 times the word \"birkhah\" in the Ḥumash, and 25 times \"shalom\" in the Ḥumash. Therefore the Priestly Blessing begins with blessing and ends with shalom. And this is: \"HaShem blesses His people with shalom.\"" "<b>Say to</b> them — plene vav, corresponding to six blessings: \"May He bless you,\" \"and may He guard you,\" \"may He illuminate,\" \"and may He be gracious to you,\" \"may He lift,\" \"and may He establish for you shalom\" — corresponding to six [mentions of] HaShem: \"Torat HaShem,\" \"edut HaShem,\" \"pikudei HaShem,\" \"mitzvot HaShem,\" \"yir'at HaShem,\" \"mishpetei HaShem.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:21:19.091972113Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}